                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Many many hours sunk into supcom. It's a bit dated now but it and it's newer version are still played competitively to this day. Despite it's age, the graphics still hold up pretty well but where it really shines is in large scale combat. It can be quite difficult to hit the unit limit it's that high and the variety of the different kinds of units really sets it out from the pack. If you're looking at this review in 2026 you already know about this game!\r\n\r\nIt's age allows it to not only run on Linux but also run pretty well. The only graphical issue I noted while playing through was the mouse cursor sometimes flickering which I think might be something to do with the age of the game rather than anything. I think this was made in the era of single-core, multi-thread applications rather than the multi-core, multi-threads we're used to these days. Sometimes it resulted in some differences in processor efficiency which I've seen reflected in a few games with that symptom.",
